flowchart TD
  Order[One confirmed timber shipment] --> Ready{Two eligible actual workers and finite warehouse cell?}
  Ready -->|no| Hold[Cargo stays aboard; event-woken reason]
  Ready -->|yes| Priority[Shared hauling priorities; no busy or higher-priority worker borrowed]
  Priority --> Reserve[One source claim, one cell and two exclusive worker roles]
  Reserve --> Fixture{Compatible fixture ready?}
  Fixture -->|no| Prepare[Actual worker reaches bay; existing shelf smoke; ready event]
  Prepare --> Access
  Fixture -->|yes| Access[Reserve clear truck aisle and paired handling stations]
  Access --> Rack[Actual timber-only S1v03 at .60/.95m; unchanged other S1 supports]
  Rack --> Pickup[Reuse bend with bounded foot-contact correction; fitted palms support one load]
  Pickup --> Joint[Ledger begins one jointly held portion]
  Joint --> Withdraw[Actual two-worker withdrawal and shoulder transition]
  Withdraw --> Ramp[Authored planted ramp gait; same fore and aft identities]
  Ramp --> Route[Complete pair and payload envelope through actual clear route]
  Route --> Stage[Clear warehouse staging; both take load into palms]
  Stage --> Place[Authored lower or upper rack placement on .60/1.75m supports]
  Place --> Commit[One joint finish and warehouse cell commit]
  Commit --> Release[Both workers leave safely; physical handover gate]
  Release --> Depart[Existing shelf securing, ramp, door and clear truck exit]
  Pose[Accepted clip and root/payload metadata] --> View[Read-only active animation views]
  Joint --> View
  Ramp --> View
  Place --> View
  View -. no stock authority .-> Joint
  Interrupted[Real interruption after lift] --> Safe{Supported warehouse deposit possible?}
  Safe -->|yes| Place
  Safe -->|no| Ground[One recoverable ground-held package; no delivered/returned/refund credit]
  Ground --> Recover[Actual later two-worker recovery route]
  Recover --> Stage
